note The io-process crate: the one place the program starts other programs (clippy's disallowed_methods keeps Command out of every other crate). Two ways in: Process::run runs a program to completion and captures its output (jj and git, through io-vcs), Process::spawn starts one with pipes for a long-lived conversation (a language server, through io-lsp). The program is looked up on PATH here, before the OS is asked, so every caller reports a missing program the same way. Failures are ProcessError values; each caller words them in its own error type.

